        Source W4514 SNOMED CT 93458008 = foreign body entering through skin at institutional residence
        during vital activities (rest, sleep, meals, personal hygiene). Target SNOMED CT 4246661 (Foreign
        body in skin) is the standard concept for the base injury and fully subsumes the injury aspect.
        Broader: target covers injury but not place/activity context. Moderate tier: best available
        standard, external-cause context lost. Parent W451 maps to 4055049 (sharp-edged object accident)
        which is too specific. Citation: Athena-local mirror.
        """
}
